// endpoint_update_remote_control_mode.proto — UpdateRemoteControlMode: turn a
// workspace's remote control on, off, or over.
//
// REMOTE CONTROL makes a workspace's session, which runs on this machine,
// reachable from claude.ai and its mobile app through the vendor's Remote
// Control bridge (shim.v1.SetSessionRemoteControl).
//
// THE MODE IS THE DAEMON'S, PERSISTED PER WORKSPACE. Unset, it defaults ON for
// a repository's main worktree and OFF for every other workspace; a request
// records the mode it leaves explicitly, so it holds across shims and daemons.
//
// A WORKSPACE IN REMOTE CONTROL KEEPS ITS SHIM UP BETWEEN KEEP-ALIVES. Its
// keep-alives go on as every workspace's do, but none is followed by a stand-
// down, so claude.ai always finds it served; its idle cutoff still hibernates
// it. Turning the mode on for a workspace with no shim starts one; turning it
// off leaves the shim up, and the next keep-alive parks it as usual.

